    explanation: 'Azure Storage Lifecycle Management allows you to define rule-based policies that automatically transition blobs to cooler tiers (Cool, Cold, Archive) or delete them based on age, last modified, or last accessed date. "Azure Storage Object Replication" asynchronously copies block blobs across storage accounts in different regions — it does not manage storage tier transitions or age-based deletions. "Azure Backup retention policies" govern how long backup snapshots are retained in vaults — they do not manage native blob tiering inside storage accounts. "Blob versioning" maintains previous states of modified blobs for recovery — it preserves versions rather than tiering or pruning data based on schedule.',
