    correctAnswerIndex: 0,
    explanation: 'Immutable Blob Storage with time-based retention policies stores data in a WORM (Write Once, Read Many) state, preventing files from being overwritten or deleted by anyone (including root/admin roles) until the retention period expires. "Azure Storage Soft Delete" retains deleted blobs in a recycle bin for a set number of days — it allows recovery after deletion, but does not prevent deletion in the first place. "Azure Blob Versioning" retains prior versions when an object is overwritten or deleted — however, versions can still be explicitly deleted unless immutability is locked. "Azure Storage Account Access Keys" provide full administrative root access to the storage account — they grant permissions rather than enforcing immutable WORM compliance.',
  ),
  Question(
